Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||07-18-2001||10:37 AM||||What is the weight of a 3.8ltr Series 2 equiped Fiero? Not with the Auto<P>I believe the series 2 SC is aluminum head motor correct?<P>Just planning , the only weight I found for the 2.8 was paired with a 3.1 , So I assume who ever wrote the artice thought the 2 motors were the same. (aluminum heads)<P>Listed weight for the 2.8/3.1 was 350lbs , which I thought was a little light considering I have a 215 cu in buick that weighs in at 320lbs complete (all aluminum)<P>To the 3.8 converted people , are you running stock spring rates in rear? Right now I have 325lbs coil overs  out back harsh for the street , just wondering if I should switch to a stiffer spring due to any weight increase.<P>Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||07-18-2001||01:28 PM||||my 3.2 felt like it was a lot more then 350 lbs with iron heads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||07-18-2001||09:12 PM||||What I've heard is that the 2.8 and N* weigh the same. I've weighed a N* longblock at either 345 or 375 lbs (don't remember which right now).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||07-18-2001||09:22 PM||||N* weighs in at 418lbs according to a few resources. The tranny weighs 300lbs!!!!<P>My reason for the 3.8SC is ease of install as compared to a N*. This is a first time swap for me. Plus for track events I would rather have a manual tranny. All a matter of what your cars purpose is.  <P>I don't think the 3.8SC would weigh anymore than a 2.8 , but I would rather go by hard #'s than "I don't think"<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||09:24 PM||||2.8 - pulley to flywheel, oilpan to intake, all accessories attached = 376 lbs||||reg||1
